// Title: Potential CommandLine Obfuscation Using Unicode Characters
// Sigma ID: e0552b19-5a83-4222-b141-b36184bb8d79
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-01-15 | Modified: 2024-09-05
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027
// Tags: detection.threat-hunting
// Description: Detects potential CommandLine obfuscation using unicode characters. Adversaries may attempt to
//   make an executable or file difficult to discover or analyze by encrypting, encoding, or
//   otherwise obfuscating its contents on the system or in transit.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.wietzebeukema.nl/blog/windows-command-line-obfuscation
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1027/T1027.md#atomic-test-6---dlp-evasion-via-sensitive-data-in-vba-macro-over-http
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules-threat-hunting/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_cli_obfuscation_unicode.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "ˣ" or ProcessCommandLine contains "˪" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ˢ" or ProcessCommandLine contains "∕" or ProcessCommandLine contains "⁄" or ProcessCommandLine contains "―" or ProcessCommandLine contains "—" or ProcessCommandLine contains " " or ProcessCommandLine contains "¯" or ProcessCommandLine contains "®" or ProcessCommandLine contains "¶"
